# Phase 3 (InlineDedupTable) vs Phase 2 (GatherDedupTable) A/B
# Issue: imazen/jxl-encoder#41 Chunk 2
# Generated: 2026-05-17
# Repo commit (this branch): 23f22d22 perf(tree_learn): wire InlineDedupTable into production gather (issue #41 chunk 2)
# Parent main: 52f8e8166cd6 perf(tree_learn): wire predictor-pruning lb-skip into find_best_predictor (issue #23 chunk 2)
# Hostname: lilith (water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM)
# Run conditions: shared with another agent running predictor_prune_c3 benches
#                 (load average ~15 during this run). The paired-statistics
#                 design averages out the shared noise — single-run absolute
#                 numbers are higher than a quiet baseline, but A/B deltas
#                 within the same paired iter are still informative.
# Command:
#   GD_EFFORTS=7,8,9 GD_SAMPLES=6 GD_WARMUP=2 GD_THREADS=8 \
#     cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder --features '__expert parallel-tree-learning' \
#       --example gather_dedup_phase3_ab
# Both arms have gather_dedup = true; only gather_dedup_phase3 differs.
# A = GatherDedupTable (Phase 2, SoA-indexed cuckoo)
# B = InlineDedupTable (Phase 3, fingerprint-cached cuckoo)
#
# Acceptance criterion (per Chunk 2 brief):
#   >= +5% wall-clock win on 1.05 MP @ e7 (8 threads) -> ship Phase 3 default-on.
#   Otherwise keep default-off, leave knob as opt-in.
#
# Result: NOT MET on 1.05 MP @ e7. Phase 3 is *slower* by +8.18% (median)
# / +6.54% (best-iter) at that exact cell. Decision: keep default-off,
# document the knob as opt-in for users on synthetic / high-dup workloads
# where the microbench's +36% to +53% gather-throughput translates to
# end-to-end wins.
#
# Bytes are byte-identical (a_bytes == b_bytes) at every cell, confirming
# the post-pre_quantize sort dedup remains the byte-determining arbiter
# regardless of which gather-time backend ran. Hash-locks therefore stay
# stable (verified separately by `cargo test --release --features
# parallel-tree-learning --test hash_lock_features` -> 36/36 pass).
#
# Columns:
#   image           - source file basename
#   megapixels      - image MP
#   effort          - encoder effort (lossless modular)
#   n               - paired samples per cell (warmup excluded)
#   a_med_ms        - Phase 2 (A) median wall-clock ms
#   b_med_ms        - Phase 3 (B) median wall-clock ms
#   delta_med_ms    - median(B-A) in ms (negative = Phase 3 faster)
#   delta_pct_med   - median(100*(B-A)/A) (negative = Phase 3 faster)
#   delta_pct_best  - 100*(min(B)-min(A))/min(A) (best-iter delta, less polluted by load spikes)
#   a_best_ms       - Phase 2 best (min) wall-clock ms
#   b_best_ms       - Phase 3 best (min) wall-clock ms
#   a_bytes         - Phase 2 output size
#   b_bytes         - Phase 3 output size
#   byte_delta_pct  - 100*(B-A)/A bytes (should be 0.0 for all cells)
